From 92a60c7156819c6bdc33c44fb56acf6116f424b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:39:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Retro tiles: tiles without the blown-out half (pos
 without its sign for fade)

With SCREEN_RES_SCALE right the shader still looked really bad on the RG DS (the owner's words): pos ran -0.5..0.5 into
fade(), which gives up to 4x brightness for a negative distance, so half of each tile was clipped towards white.
pos = abs(pos) once dir has the sign. Only the shipped .frag changes: the NNDDSS source isn't in the repo.

Test: tools/shaders/tests/conv-dfx-test.py checks it (fails on the file before this). On device (RG DS, BananaOS 0.5.3,
Mali-G52, shtest's colour bars at 2x): white-clipped pixels 9.2% -> 2.0%, real tiles with dark gaps; darker overall (mean
122 -> 69), gaps a little uneven at the RG DS's 2.5x. Through BananaDS's menu in a game, on the owner's screen: "good
enough". Not checked on the Plus, the panel it was made for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01StxwK2dxEyPmeRLuqBRYJ3
(cherry picked from commit 87e45514695da0839aaa8d77d73a0aa73f1a2428)
