From a76031a4d2660851c281788f8495eb6c87303e49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:12:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Quit-save keeps the previous resume state if the new one
 doesn't finish

SIGUSR1 deleted DSFLIP_RESUME_FILE before DraStic had written a replacement.
A save that timed out (5 s) or failed (full disk) then quit with no resume
file at all, including the last good one. The rename hook already replaces
that file only once the new state is complete, so the early unlink is gone.

Co-authored-by: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 33a798c94f17637946319d2df9f2623ff848c434)
---
 .github/workflows/build.yml |  2 +
 docs/INTEGRATION.md         |  2 +-
 src/resume.c                |  9 +++-
 tools/README.md             |  1 +
 tools/resume-keep-test.c    | 83 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 94 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tools/resume-keep-test.c

diff --git a/.github/workflows/build.yml b/.github/workflows/build.yml
index b7d521d..ae7b727 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/build.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build.yml
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@ jobs:
             llvm-nm -D --defined-only $L | grep -q " $s\$" || { echo "hook $s missing"; exit 1; }
           done
           sh -n runner/superdrastic-run && sh -n runner/superdrastic-update
+          clang -O2 -Wall -Wextra -o /tmp/resume-keep-test tools/resume-keep-test.c src/resume.c -ldl -lpthread
+          /tmp/resume-keep-test
       - name: Package
         run: sh package.sh
       - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
diff --git a/docs/INTEGRATION.md b/docs/INTEGRATION.md
index e8e9473..50ea801 100644
--- a/docs/INTEGRATION.md
+++ b/docs/INTEGRATION.md
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ Exit hotkeys usually kill DraStic (`kill -9`), which loses the game's place. Sen
 `DSFLIP_RESUME_FILE`: SuperDrastic presses DraStic's own "save state" control (the joystick button `drastic.cfg`
 maps to it), writes the savestate to that file instead of one of the player's slots, and exits with SIGKILL (status
 137, as a hotkey kill). Measured on the RG DS: ~0.8 s for the save. A second SIGUSR1, or no savestate within 5 s,
-exits at once. Start the game next time with `DSFLIP_RESUME_LOAD=1` as well: once it runs, SuperDrastic presses
+exits at once; a resume file already there is left as it was if that save doesn't finish. Start the game next time with `DSFLIP_RESUME_LOAD=1` as well: once it runs, SuperDrastic presses
 "load state" with DraStic's lookup pointed at the resume file, shows a "Resumed" pop-up and deletes the file.
 
 Keep the file in DraStic's `savestates/` folder (a rename, no copy) and name it anything but `<game>_<digit>.dss`.
diff --git a/src/resume.c b/src/resume.c
index c2187cc..e8c03d5 100644
--- a/src/resume.c
+++ b/src/resume.c
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
 // DraStic's savestate file calls.
 // DSFLIP_RESUME_ON_QUIT=0: only SIGUSR1 saves; the in-game menu's Quit and the exit combos quit at once, as without a
 // file (a frontend whose own quick resume is off, that still saves the game before a power-off of its own).
+// The previous resume file stays until DraStic's rename replaces it, so a save that doesn't finish (the 5 s timeout,
+// a full disk) leaves the last good state in place.
 #define _GNU_SOURCE
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <errno.h>
@@ -258,7 +260,9 @@ static void *save_thread(void *a) {
     long long t0 = now_ms();
